userenv: Add a stub for DeriveAppContainerSidFromAppContainerName.

Firefox 153 ESR and later delay-load this function when they set up the
sandbox of a media helper process (the app container "fx.sb.cdm..."). Without
the export the delay-load fails with exception 0xc06d007f and the whole
browser goes down, for instance a few seconds after opening youtube.com.

With a stub that reports E_NOTIMPL, like CreateAppContainerProfile next to it,
Firefox logs that the helper could not be launched and carries on. Returning
the real SID instead makes Firefox go further into the app container setup,
where it fails one of its own checks, so the stub is deliberate.

Status: not yet sent to WineHQ.
---
--- a/dlls/userenv/userenv.spec
+++ b/dlls/userenv/userenv.spec
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 @ stdcall CreateAppContainerProfile(wstr wstr wstr ptr long ptr)
 @ stdcall CreateEnvironmentBlock(ptr ptr long)
+@ stdcall DeriveAppContainerSidFromAppContainerName(wstr ptr)
 @ stdcall DestroyEnvironmentBlock(ptr)
 @ stdcall EnterCriticalPolicySection(long)
 @ stdcall ExpandEnvironmentStringsForUserA(ptr str ptr long)
--- a/dlls/userenv/userenv_main.c
+++ b/dlls/userenv/userenv_main.c
@@ -696,3 +696,10 @@
 
     return E_NOTIMPL;
 }
+
+HRESULT WINAPI DeriveAppContainerSidFromAppContainerName(const WCHAR *container_name, SID **container_sid)
+{
+    FIXME("(%s, %p): stub\n", debugstr_w(container_name), container_sid);
+
+    return E_NOTIMPL;
+}
